# Sample Dashboard — Annotated Reference

These notes explain the patterns found in the verified production dashboards
(Promotion_Tactic_Accrual_Summary.json, Promotion_Tactic_Accrual_Dashboard.json,
Accrued_Month_End_Report.json). Use these patterns when authoring dashboards for
orgs that use Data Cloud datasets or aggregateflex-style steps.

---

## Key differences from storm-org style dashboards

| Thing | storm-org style | Standard production style |
|---|---|---|
| Step type | `saql` | `aggregateflex` (compact form 2.0) |
| Query format | SAQL string in `query` field | Structured `query.sources[]` array |
| Dataset reference | `datasets:[{id, name, url}]` | `cdpObjects:["datasetApiName"]` + `datasets:[]` |
| Data source | CRMA datasets | Data Cloud (DLM) objects |
| numColumns | 49 (storm anomaly) | **12** (real-world default) |
| text widget body | plain `text` string | `richTextContent` array |

---

## gridLayout — numColumns is 12

Production CRMA dashboards use `numColumns: 12`. This is the CRMA canvas default.
Column positions (0–11) and colspans must add up within 12.

```json
"gridLayouts": [{
  "name": "Default",
  "numColumns": 12,
  "rowHeight": "normal",
  "style": {
    "backgroundColor": "#F2F6FA",
    "cellSpacingX": 8,
    "cellSpacingY": 8,
    "gutterColor": "#C5D3E0",
    "fit": "original",
    "alignmentX": "left",
    "alignmentY": "top"
  },
  "pages": [{
    "label": "Untitled",
    "name": "<uuid>",
    "navigationHidden": false,
    "widgets": [
      { "name": "chart_1",  "row": 1, "column": 0, "rowspan": 8, "colspan": 4,
        "widgetStyle": { "borderEdges": [] } },
      { "name": "table_1",  "row": 1, "column": 4, "rowspan": 8, "colspan": 8,
        "widgetStyle": { "borderEdges": [] } },
      { "name": "filterpanel_1", "row": 0, "column": 0, "rowspan": 1, "colspan": 2,
        "widgetStyle": {
          "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF", "borderColor": "#747474",
          "borderEdges": ["all"], "borderRadius": 4, "borderWidth": 1
        }}
    ]
  }],
  "version": 1,
  "selectors": []
}]
```

